# The Lion-Turtle ({1}{G}{U}, 3/6 reach, vigilance): "When The Lion-Turtle enters, you gain 3 life" (Bot1 20 -> 23). "{T}: Add one mana of any
# color" pays for Bot1's Octopus Forms (U, instant Lessons that untap their target): the Turtle taps for {U} and casts a Form on itself (exactly one {U} is added).
# "Can't attack ... unless there are three or more Lesson cards in your graveyard" (CR 508.1c): the attack is refused with 0, 1 and 2
# Lessons, one on each of turns 3, 5 and 7 (a refusal spends its turn; Black Lotus in the graveyard is no Lesson), and allowed on turn 9
# with 3: the Turtle deals 3 and, with vigilance, stays untapped. Bot1's Memnite is on the battlefield so that attacking is on offer at
# all (the refusals need a prompt); it stays home.

